<td align="center" valign="top" width="60%">

<table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0">
<tr bgcolor="#e0c0a0">
<td align="left" valign="top"><font face="helvetica" color="000000" size="2">

<img border="1" align="left" valign="top" height="109" width="79" src="http://web.archive.org/web/20021002230149im_/http://www.eskimo.com/img/pics/nanook.jpg">
	
<p>
I'm sorry we couldn't meet under better circumstances.  The loss of a
valued web page can be tough.
</p>
<p>
As long as you are here, let me introduce myself.  My name is Robert
Dinse, also known as &quot;Nanook&quot;.  You can e-mail me at
<a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20021002230149/mailto:nanook@eskimo.com">nanook@eskimo.com</a>.
</p>
<p>
I started Eskimo North as a single line BBS in 1982.  Over the years it
has gradually evolved into the full featured Internet service providing
access and host services such as web hosting, e-mail, and Usenet News. 
</p>
<p>
We have not been acquired.  We have not acquired or merged with other
services.  Eskimo North remains independently owned and operated.  The
emphasis here is on our service, not on wheeling and dealing.  There are
no phone menus here, nor is there any triage at the help desk. Every
customer is important to us. 
</p>

<p>
While you are here, please take advantage of our <a <a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20021002230149/http://www.eskimo.com/newuser.html">two-week <font size="3"><blink><b>free</b></blink></font> trial</a> of our
<a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20021002230149/http://www.eskimo.com/services/dial.html">56k</a>,
<a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20021002230149/http://www.eskimo.com/services/dial.html">dual 56k</a>,
<a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20021002230149/http://www.eskimo.com/services/isdn.html">ISDN</a>, and
<a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20021002230149/http://www.eskimo.com/services/shells.html">remote shell</a> 
services.  I believe that you will not be disappointed.
</p>

</td>
</tr>

